/-!
# E.4: Values of a for binary representations

The development supplies restriction and isomorphism transport of the actual
fixed-space parameter, the solvable reduction from E.3.40, and the corank-family
constructions for the generating-family argument. All quotients and group
embeddings are intrinsic. The even-order qualification in E.4.1 and the local
quotient convention in E.4.2 are documented in the owning modules.

The unconditional solvable theorem still needs E.3.40. The E.4.2 bound, the
Mathieu generating families, and the concrete M₂₃ code/cocode restrictions are
also outstanding. No numbered source theorem is asserted from these partial
results; final assembly remains in this section.

Source: Aschbacher–Smith, combined manuscript of 1 March 2004, §E.4,
printed pp. 240–242 (PDF pp. 251–253).
-/
